- **T005 surfaced a latent defect.** `input-remapper-control --command stop` exits 4 ("Did not find any input device") when the DualSense is not connected, and `--restore` propagated it, so `ExecStopPost` marked `zuzz-media.service` **failed after every clean stop**. The pre-existing `--restore` also propagated this status, so it was latent rather than newly introduced, but it was reachable any time the browser was stopped with the controller off. `--restore` is now best-effort: it warns and exits 0, because a controller that is not connected has no remapping left to undo.
- Verified after the fix: a full `stop` then `start` cycle leaves `zuzz-media.service` `inactive` then `active`, Firefox relaunches in kiosk, `media-home.service` stays disabled and inactive throughout, no Kodi process ever appears, and SSH stays active.
